Z||000000||trigger||11-29-2000||07:12 PM||||I noticed there is a spare wiring harness behind the radio in my 88 coupe 4 cyl auto.  it is like a hollow plastic box with one end off of it.  It has little pokey rods sticking up inside of it.  it's black.  I was wondering if anybody knows what it's for.<BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||11-29-2000||10:56 PM||||Beats me! Does your radio work? There is a connector behind the radio, just like the one that plugs into the factory radio, but it should be hooked up to another plug going to the speakers.||||reg||1
